or": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01LeXfC3njxofg91yJnbLBYe", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 2, "runtime_actions": ["retry_after_429"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 379269, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01LeXfC3njxofg91yJnbLBYe", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 383849, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch. CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` says in its comment that it uses banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212). The code actually rounded halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), so 2.665 became 2.67 instead of the 2.66 the test expects.\n- **The fix:** I changed the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` on branch `fix/money-banker-rounding` (commit 08d3cd5986). That was the only change.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nThe advisory lookup tool didn't recognise FIN-212, so I couldn't read the rule directly. I relied on the comment in the code and the test, which both say to use ROUND_HALF_EVEN.\n\nI haven't merged the PR, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01DzBnHkNLoYxjE2wq4R5csN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01FQwQGzvs6jmSh33YoWeWHq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01QJqRWh75MSTF2yKqqfwPbh", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01268hkHBN8WoFB3E5oKwBeT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-banker-rounding"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01DJR8S4UsYa7wgKHHZFYvLu", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01QZjFxfGbQSH1q4ZnhtbQqv", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-banker-rounding-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01GM6uA7tRRt5y9EyHeF4F1y", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01LeXfC3njxofg91yJnbLBYe", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "`round_money` in `src/money.py` was documented as using banker's rounding (FIN-212) but actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, causing `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` to fail in the nightly build.\n\nThis switches the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch. CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` says in its comment that it uses banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212). The code actually rounded halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), so 2.665 became 2.67 instead of the 2.66 the test expects.\n- **The fix:** I changed the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` on branch `fix/money-banker-rounding` (commit 08d3cd5986). That was the only change.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nThe advisory lookup tool didn't recognise FIN-212, so I couldn't read the rule directly. I relied on the comment in the code and the test, which both say to use ROUND_HALF_EVEN.\n\nI haven't merged the PR, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}